 r←eventNumber name;i
⍝ The event NUMBER for an event name, or the name unchanged if it has none.
⍝
⍝ ⎕WC reports events numerically to APL, whatever form was used to register
⍝ them -- verified against Dyalog 20.0, where ('Event'(1 2)'CB') and
⍝ ('Event' 'MouseDown' 'CB') both deliver 2⊃msg as the integer 1, ⎕DR 83.
⍝
⍝ Legacy code depends on that and tests it arithmetically:
⍝
⍝     →0⍴⍨2=2⊃MSG                        a mouse handler ignoring MouseUp
⍝     R←61=2⊃⎕DQ'QUESTION_MSGBOX'        a Query box asking which button
⍝
⍝ Given a character vector those comparisons produce a boolean VECTOR, and the
⍝ surrounding guard then fails with RANK ERROR. So both routes back into user
⍝ code -- the callback message built by processEvent and the result returned by
⍝ ∆DQ -- have to convert, which is why this lives in one place.
⍝
⍝ 'onXxx' handler spellings are accepted, and matching is case-insensitive.
 r←name
 :If isChar name
     i←(⎕C EVENTNAMES)⍳⊂⎕C(2×'on'≡⎕C 2↑name)↓name
     :If i≤≢EVENTNUMS
         r←i⊃EVENTNUMS
     :EndIf
 :EndIf
